1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,550
This is CatatMD.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,510
It turns a GP consultation into a clinical
note the doctor can review.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,128
Everything you'll see here is synthetic:
no real patient appears.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,081
The doctor registers a patient and starts
a consultation from the profile.

5
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:27,396
With the patient's consent, given for this
visit only, CatatMD listens.

6
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,563
Doctor: Good morning. Please,

7
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:33,600
have a seat. Before we start, can I
confirm your IC number?

8
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:41,030
Patient: My IC is 900412086543.

9
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:44,430
Doctor: Thank you, Puan Siti. What brings
you in today?

10
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,320
Patient: I've had a cough for three days
now,

11
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:50,560
and since yesterday my throat is really
sore.

12
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:52,820
Doctor: I'm sorry to hear that.

13
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,480
Doctor: Are you coughing anything up?

14
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:58,930
Patient: Some white phlegm. But this
morning I noticed a

15
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:02,450
few streaks of blood in my phlegm, and
that worried me.

16
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,043
The transcript builds live, turn by turn,

17
00:01:05,093 --> 00:01:08,465
and the safety panel suggests what to ask
next.

18
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,999
One click analyses the visit.

19
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:21,566
Before any text leaves the server, names
and identity numbers become tokens.

20
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,810
The model only ever sees the tokens,

21
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:27,261
and the real details come back on the
return trip.

22
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,896
The doctor reviews three panels side by
side:

23
00:01:34,946 --> 00:01:38,697
the transcript, the structured note, and
clinical safety.

24
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,150
Red flags come from deterministic rules
first.

25
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:47,034
The model can add candidates for review,
but it can never remove a rule's hit.

26
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:52,351
The checklist ties each field to the words
that support it.

27
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,272
Suggestions cite guideline IDs from a
fixed corpus,

28
00:01:57,322 --> 00:02:00,600
so a made-up reference cannot reach the
screen.

29
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:13,463
CatatAI answers questions about the visit,
and can propose an edit.

30
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:26,033
Nothing changes until the doctor applies
it.

31
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,923
The doctor dictates the prescription.

32
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:41,250
Doctor: Paracetamol, two tablets four
times a day for five days.

33
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:46,640
Doctor: Benzydamine gargle, 15 mL three
times a day for five days.

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,298
CatatMD parses each line into dose,
frequency and duration,

35
00:02:54,348 --> 00:02:58,050
and saves only the lines the doctor
confirms.

36
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,535
Nothing is ever approved by default.

37
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:06,579
The doctor acknowledges the red flags and
approves the note.

38
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,383
The finished record exports as a
consultation report.

39
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,450
CatatMD drafts.

40
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,149
The doctor decides.
